{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_abtbuhpsvbjx2drtph5bq6gnoaw5xo3v4xoyrlbcji6ij2ix3d2q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 101 tests pass across all 9 modules. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nI created comprehensive Rust test files in `src/bin/` that mirror the C test suite for each module:\n\n- **test_annotation.rs** (8 tests) — Tests for `pgn_annotation_from_string` (single-symbol annotations like `!`, `??`, `?!`), `pgn_annotation_nag_from_string` (NAG annotations like `$0`, `$19`, `$420`), and `Display` (which acts as `pgn_annotation_to_string`).\n- **test_check.rs** (8 tests) — Tests `__pgn_check_from_string` for `+`, `++`, `#`, empty, no-check, and trailing characters; checks the `i8` repr values.\n- **test_comments.rs** (13 tests) — Tests `PgnComment::new`/`from_string`, nested comments, `PgnComments::push`/`poll`/`get_first_after_alternative_index`.\n- **test_coordinate.rs** (4 tests) — Tests `pgn_coordinate_file_as_index` for both lower- and uppercase, plus default and constants.\n- **test_metadata.rs** (8 tests) — Tests `PgnMetadata::insert`/`get`/`delete`/`from_string`/`from_string_with_consumption`.\n- **test_moves.rs** (34 tests) — Tests `PgnMove::from`/`from_string_with_consumption` for pawns, knights, queens, castling, en passant, ambiguous moves, NAG annotations; tests `Display` for all formatting variations; tests `PgnMoves::from` parsing of full move sequences with comments and alternatives.\n- **test_pgn.rs** (6 tests) — Tests `Pgn::new`/`parse_metadata`/`parse_score`/`parse_move`/`parse_moves`/`parse` with the full PGN test from `c_src/tests/pgn.c`.\n- **test_piece.rs** (3 tests) — Tests `From<char>`, `Display`, and the `u8` repr values.\n- **test_score.rs** (4 tests) — Tests valid/invalid scores, consumption tracking, and `Display`.\n- **test_utils.rs** (13 tests) — Tests `PgnBuffer` (append/concat/reset/equals/detach) and `pgn_cursor_*` functions.\n\n## Translation Bug Fix\n\nI found and fixed a real translation bug in `src/annotation.rs`. The C `pgn_annotation_t` is an enum but stores arbitrary integer NAG values (`$19`, `$69`, `$420`, etc.). The Rust translation used a fixed enum that lost values outside `-1..=6` (e.g. `PgnAnnotation::from(19_i8)` produced `Unknown`). This broke the C test that asserts `annotation == 69` and `annotation == 420`.\n\nI refactored `PgnAnnotation` from a fixed enum into a `#[repr(transparent)] struct PgnAnnotation(pub i32)` with associated constants (`Unknown`, `Null`, `GoodMove`, ...) preserving the existing call sites. I also fixed `Display` to format any non-standard value as `$N`, and updated `PgnMove::Display` in `src/moves.rs` to mirror the C trailing-NAG logic (`> DUBIOUS_MOVE || == NULL`).\n\nTotal: **101 tests across 9 modules — all passing.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":794,"cache_read_input_tokens":147565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":794,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dde47fb5-252b-4b3d-bfcb-2b8a4337ad06","uuid":"7a87ee2c-e793-492e-997e-ec0d142a7c4d"}
